# helm-unittest suites are development-time only. Without this they are packaged into the
# released chart: `helm package` includes every file under the chart dir that is not ignored,
# and there was no .helmignore here at all before (verified: the file did not exist).
tests/

# The ANNOTATED pins file is development-time only; the chart reads the generated data-only
# files/component-pins.min.yaml instead (see _helpers.tpl). helm embeds the entire chart in its
# release record, and a release Secret's data may not exceed 1 MiB DECODED. krateo-057 proved it:
# revision 546 reached 1,047,684 bytes with 892 to spare and revision 547 was refused outright
# ("data: Too long"). This file is 740,859 bytes, 97.6% of it comment prose; excluding it takes the
# packaged archive from 519,968 to 246,583 bytes. The comments stay in git, beside the pins they
# explain, which is where they get read at pin time.
files/component-pins.yaml
